Also pssible to do it from command line:

gh auth login                    * login
git init                         * initialize repository
git remote -v                    * check current remote URL
gh repo create my-repo --private       * create new private repository

git branch
git branch -m master main       *rename branch name
git remote add origin https://github.com/oetjensa/EXAMPLE.git   * link to GitHub repository    
git add .                       * stage files
git commit -m 'file'            * commit changes
git push -u origin main   * with -u don't need the origin main anymore
git pull                       * update local repository
